For the payload, the shell needs to be made of styrofoam.
We also need handwarmers to keep the internal components functioning, and we need a small slit in the foam box for the DHT22 to slide into for temperature readings.
The BMP280 can stay completely in the shell though, as we will only use it for pressure, which will equalize through styrofoam.
The GPS module can stay inside the box, as it's signals pass through styrofoam.
